// Title: Suspicious Interactive PowerShell as SYSTEM
// Sigma ID: 5b40a734-99b6-4b98-a1d0-1cea51a08ab2
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-12-07 | Modified: 2022-08-13
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.001
// Description: Detects the creation of files that indicator an interactive use of PowerShell in the SYSTEM user
//   context
// False positives:
//   - Administrative activity
//   - PowerShell scripts running as SYSTEM user
// References:
//   - https://jpcertcc.github.io/ToolAnalysisResultSheet/details/PowerSploit_Invoke-Mimikatz.htm
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_system_interactive_powershell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath in~ ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\config\\systemprofile\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\PSReadLine\\ConsoleHost_history.txt", "C:\\Windows\\System32\\config\\systemprofile\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\StartupProfileData-Interactive")
